WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:03.836
-This week, President Trump
violated the Iran deal,

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:05.237
and a CIA director was grilled

00:00:05.237 --> 00:00:06.940
under past involvement
in torture.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.374
Meanwhile, Trump supporters

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:10.443
were calling for him
to win the Nobel Peace Prize.

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.412
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:17.016
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:19.586
Trump's attempts
at diplomacy with North Korea

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:21.587
are a positive development.

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:22.788
And if the North and South

00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:24.691
manage to broker
a peace deal with Trump's help,

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:25.992
that would be historic.

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:28.093
But now some people
are taking it five steps further

00:00:28.093 --> 00:00:30.696
and insisting that Trump
deserves the Nobel Peace Prize,

00:00:30.696 --> 00:00:33.066
and he was asked about it
yesterday at the White House.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.237
-Everyone thinks so,
but I would never say it.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:38.604
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:42.241
You know what I want to do?
I want to get it finished.

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:44.944
The prize I want
is victory for the world.

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.346
-Victory for the world?

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:47.380
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.148
He doesn't sound
like a Nobel laureate.

00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:52.018
He sounds like a movie president
fighting an alien invasion.

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:53.386
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:57.390
"I want victory for the world
against the space bugs,

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.826
one of whom
won't leave me alone."

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.294
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:02.996
Shoo, space bug!"

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:04.330
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.198
And, again, diplomacy
with North Korea is good,

00:01:06.198 --> 00:01:08.734
but this is still the same guy
who wanted to ban Muslims,

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:10.036
called Mexicans rapists,

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:11.637
said we should
kill the families of terrorists,

00:01:11.637 --> 00:01:12.871
and said
he wanted fewer immigrants

00:01:12.871 --> 00:01:14.073
from Africa and Haiti.

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:16.041
If he won a Nobel, his speech

00:01:16.041 --> 00:01:18.711
would be the first in history
with an NC-17 rating.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.146
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.181
But, okay, let's hear budding
Nobel laureate Donald Trump

00:01:22.181 --> 00:01:25.118
answer questions in detail
about his upcoming summit

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:27.153
with North Korean Leader
Kim Jong-un.

00:01:30.689 --> 00:01:33.926
-Everything can be scuttled.
Everything can be scuttled.

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:36.062
Doesn't mean --
A lot of things can happen.

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:37.529
A lot of good things can happen.

00:01:37.529 --> 00:01:39.432
A lot of bad things can happen.

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.233
-Wow. Soaring words.

00:01:41.233 --> 00:01:44.503 line:0%
You get a more specific answer
from Gmail's auto-reply.

00:01:44.503 --> 00:01:48.574 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:51.777
Also, there's a chance

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:53.279
he doesn't know
what "scuttle" means.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:54.380
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.584
"Anything can be scuttled.

00:01:57.584 --> 00:01:59.185
Bananas."

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:01.087
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:04.023
"Sidewalks --
you can scuttle them."

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:06.258
And on the same day
Trump was asked about

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:08.194
the Nobel Peace Prize,
his nominee for CIA Director,

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.196
Gina Haspel,
was being grilled in the Senate

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:12.598
over her role
in the CIA's torture program,

00:02:12.598 --> 00:02:15.968
including the time she ran
a CIA black site in Thailand,

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:17.604
where detainees
were waterboarded

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:19.606
in violation
of U.S. and international law.

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:21.907
Yesterday, Haspel
was repeatedly pressed

00:02:21.907 --> 00:02:23.576
on whether torture was immoral,

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:25.711
and she refused
to answer the question.

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:27.480
-Do you believe
that the previous

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:32.952
interrogation techniques
were immoral?

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:38.057
-Senator, I believe
that CIA officers

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:39.391
to whom you referred --

00:02:39.391 --> 00:02:40.960
-It's a yes-or-no answer.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.530
-Do you believe, in hindsight,

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:46.032
that those techniques
were immoral?

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.168
-Senator, what I believe,
sitting here today,

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:51.304
is that I support
the higher moral standard

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:52.939
we have decided
to hold ourselves to.

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:55.241
-Can you please
answer the question?

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:56.843
-Senator, I think
I've answered the question.

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:57.877
-No, you've not.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:59.979
-I love -- I love when they say,

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:03.016
"I answered your question"
as if it's a Jedi mind trick.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:04.249
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.249 --> 00:03:06.052
"These are not the answers
you're looking for."

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:07.320
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.455
In another revealing exchange,
Haspel was pressed

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:11.758
on whether she would follow
an order from President Trump

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:13.492
to illegally waterboard
a detainee,

00:03:13.492 --> 00:03:15.894
and her immediate answer
was not reassuring.

00:03:15.894 --> 00:03:22.235
-If the CIA has
a high-value terrorism suspect

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:26.005
in its custody,
and the President gave you

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:30.076
a direct order to waterboard

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:34.414
that suspect,
what would you do?

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:37.416
-Senator, I would advise --

00:03:37.416 --> 00:03:40.486
I do not believe the President
would ask me to do that.

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:43.222
-First of all, moving forward,
no one is allowed to say,

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:45.224
"I do not believe
the President would..."

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:46.358
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.358 --> 00:03:49.028
...followed
by any terrible thing.

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.263
If you don't believe --

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:52.965
[ Applause ]

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:55.735
If you don't believe
the President would shove a nun,

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.770
you're not trying hard enough

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:01.374
to envision a situation where
a nun would be in his way.

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:03.509
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:05.578
And second of all,
did you miss this?

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:07.346
-I would
bring back waterboarding,

00:04:07.346 --> 00:04:09.582
and I'd bring back
a hell of a lot worse

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:10.750
than waterboarding.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.352
If I say, "Do it,"
they're gonna do it.

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:14.153
That's what leadership
is all about.

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:17.089
-No. "If I say, 'Do it,'
they're gonna do it"

00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:18.324
is not leadership.

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:20.593
That's the Westminster Dog Show.

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:22.661
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.661 --> 00:04:25.297
And now, to be fair
to President Trump,

00:04:25.297 --> 00:04:28.300
President Obama also nominated
a CIA Director, John Brennan,

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.903
who was a defender of torture,
so this isn't unique to Trump.

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:33.505
It's something we all have
to eventually reckon with.

00:04:33.505 --> 00:04:35.308
And while Trump's
nominee for CIA director

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:38.043
was refusing to disavow her role
in an illegal torture program,

00:04:38.043 --> 00:04:40.980
Trump was also busy violating
the Iran nuclear deal.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.349
Trump has long railed
against the Iran deal,

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:46.018
but he doesn't actually have a
coherent argument against it.

00:04:46.018 --> 00:04:48.388
All he does
is mock the people who wrote it,

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:49.922
like former
Secretary of State John Kerry.

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:51.857
Kerry famously
got in a cycling accident

00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:53.359
while he was
negotiating the deal,

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:55.227
and that's apparently
the one thing

00:04:55.227 --> 00:04:56.429
Trump knows about it,

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:58.730
because he keeps mentioning it
over and over,

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:01.934
as he did yet again
at an NRA conference last week.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:04.737
-The former administration...

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:08.274
[ Audience booing ]

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:13.612
...as represented
by John Kerry...

00:05:13.612 --> 00:05:15.815
[ Audience booing ]

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:18.517
Not the best negotiator
we've ever seen.

00:05:18.517 --> 00:05:21.520
He never walked away
from the table

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.589
except to be
in that bicycle race

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.024
where he fell and broke his leg.
That's the only...

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:26.625
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:27.960
I said, "Don't tell him
you broke your leg.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.929
Just stay inside, say
you don't want to negotiate.

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:31.430
You'll make a much better deal."

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:32.431
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.431 --> 00:05:34.400
But he broke his leg.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.203
And I learned from that,

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:40.639
at 73 years old,
you never go into bicycle race.

00:05:40.639 --> 00:05:42.141
Okay, just don't.

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:43.909
-Yeah, I don't think
anyone was worried

00:05:43.909 --> 00:05:45.545
you'd get into a bicycle race.

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:46.946
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:49.582
Mostly because
they don't allow golf carts.

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:51.450
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:54.654
It is so, so Donald Trump

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:57.189
that he keeps harping
on Kerry breaking his leg.

00:05:57.189 --> 00:05:59.225
Trump is like the guy
you went to high school with

00:05:59.225 --> 00:06:02.127
who never forgets
your most embarrassing moment.

00:06:02.127 --> 00:06:03.529
You see him
at a reunion and say,

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:06.332
"Hey, there -- Dale McCaffrey.
I sat behind you in math."

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:09.135
"I remember when you crapped
your pants at prom."

00:06:09.135 --> 00:06:10.536
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:12.572
"Look, everyone --
it's Crappy Dale!"

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:14.039
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.039 --> 00:06:16.442
And Trump's comments about Iran
have been mostly incoherent,

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:18.510
but his inner circle
has been much clearer.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:20.012
They want regime change.

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:22.582
For example, Trump's
newest lawyer, Rudy Giuliani,

00:06:22.582 --> 00:06:24.583
who made that
very clear over the weekend

00:06:24.583 --> 00:06:27.386
in a speech he gave to opponents
of the Iranian regime.

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:29.122
-We've got a president
who's tough,

00:06:29.122 --> 00:06:34.893
a president who doesn't listen
to the people who are naysayers,

00:06:34.893 --> 00:06:36.162
and a president

00:06:36.162 --> 00:06:39.765
that is as committed
to regime change as we are.

00:06:39.765 --> 00:06:43.635
-Why is the President's lawyer
giving foreign-policy speeches?

00:06:43.635 --> 00:06:45.737
The highest job
he ever held was mayor.

00:06:45.737 --> 00:06:47.306
His idea of foreign policy

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:49.709
was having lunch
with the mayor of Hoboken.

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:51.210
[ Laughter ]

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:54.113
Also, if anyone should be
worried about regime change,

00:06:54.113 --> 00:06:55.381
it's Rudy Giuliani.

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:56.715
Based on how things are going,

00:06:56.715 --> 00:07:00.119
I guess he has a week left
in his job, tops.

00:07:00.119 --> 00:07:02.855
When he goes on Fox News,
they should introduce him as

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:04.423 line:0%
the Season Finale
of Rudy Giuliani.

00:07:04.423 --> 00:07:07.293
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:10.095
And Giuliani...
[ Applause continues ]

00:07:10.095 --> 00:07:12.531
Giuliani is not the only one
of Trump's associate's

00:07:12.531 --> 00:07:14.166
who has openly called
for regime change.

00:07:14.166 --> 00:07:16.002
Just take Trump's
National Security Adviser,

00:07:16.002 --> 00:07:18.770
John Bolton,
who said this just last year.

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:22.641
-The declared policy
of the United States of America

00:07:22.641 --> 00:07:24.110
should be the overthrow

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:26.646
of the Mullah's regime
in Tehran.

00:07:26.646 --> 00:07:29.214
-Now I don't know if Trump will
actually listen to John Bolton,

00:07:29.214 --> 00:07:31.550
but there's hope,
because as you may recall,

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:33.286
Trump was originally reluctant
to hire Bolton,

00:07:33.286 --> 00:07:35.521
not because of his insane
foreign-policy ideas

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:38.123
but because of Bolton's
brush-like mustache,

00:07:38.123 --> 00:07:39.358
with one associate saying,

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:41.360
"Donald was not going
to like that mustache."

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:42.928
[ Laughter ]

00:07:42.928 --> 00:07:44.563
So if Trump is thinking

00:07:44.563 --> 00:07:46.898
of taking Bolton's advice
on Iran,

00:07:46.898 --> 00:07:48.033
I would just like to say,

00:07:48.033 --> 00:07:49.335
"Mr. President,
look at that mustache."

00:07:49.335 --> 00:07:50.669
[ Laughter ]

00:07:50.669 --> 00:07:52.838
Can you really trust a guy
with a mustache like that?

00:07:52.838 --> 00:07:55.374
He looks like evil Mark Twain.

00:07:55.374 --> 00:07:56.509
[ Laughter ]

00:07:56.509 --> 00:07:59.178
John Bolton is Dark Twain.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:59.178 --> 00:08:00.880
He looks like
he walked into a barbershop

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:03.115
and said, "Give me
half a Wilford Brimley."

00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:04.817
[ Laughter ]

00:08:04.817 --> 00:08:07.286
So, Trump is surrounding himself
with people who made clear

00:08:07.286 --> 00:08:08.721
they want regime change in Iran,

00:08:08.721 --> 00:08:10.956
which undercuts
one of the central claims

00:08:10.956 --> 00:08:13.893
of Trump's presidential campaign
that he -- he --

00:08:13.893 --> 00:08:15.360
was the anti-war candidate.

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:16.795
As you might recall,
he repeatedly

00:08:16.795 --> 00:08:18.230
went out of his way
to claim, falsely,

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:20.198
that he was opposed
to the Iraq war,

00:08:20.198 --> 00:08:22.702
which he said, over
and over again, was a disaster.

00:08:22.702 --> 00:08:24.370
-George Bush made a mistake.

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:26.772
We can make mistakes.
But that one was a beauty.

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:29.041
We should've never been in Iraq.

00:08:29.041 --> 00:08:31.310
We have destabilized
the Middle East.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:34.580
They lied. They said there were
weapons of mass destruction,

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:36.848
there were none,
and they knew there were none.

00:08:36.848 --> 00:08:38.350
Look at the mess we have.

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:41.219
We've destabilized the
Middle East, and it's a mess.

00:08:41.219 --> 00:08:42.922
Had we not done anything,

00:08:42.922 --> 00:08:46.392
had our politicians gone to
the beach and enjoyed the sun,

00:08:46.392 --> 00:08:48.961
we would be in a lot better
position than we are right now.

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:50.529
What we've done is incredible.

00:08:50.529 --> 00:08:52.164
If we would've --
If our presidents

00:08:52.164 --> 00:08:55.267
would've just stayed home
and gone to the beach

00:08:55.267 --> 00:08:57.102
or even gone out
and played golf,

00:08:57.102 --> 00:09:00.238
every single day,
played two rounds a day --

00:09:00.238 --> 00:09:03.542
okay? --
which Obama almost does.

00:09:03.542 --> 00:09:05.810
-Obama played two rounds a day?

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:07.179
Trump plays so much golf,

00:09:07.179 --> 00:09:10.049
I wouldn't be surprised
if he played during meetings.

00:09:10.049 --> 00:09:11.050
[ Laughter ]

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:14.453
"Rudy, open wide.

00:09:14.453 --> 00:09:15.621
Hole in one.

00:09:15.621 --> 00:09:16.989
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:16.989 --> 00:09:19.225
Hole in one."

00:09:19.225 --> 00:09:20.626
[ Applause ]

00:09:20.626 --> 00:09:22.394
And yet Trump and his allies
are now repeating

00:09:22.394 --> 00:09:24.296
the same mistakes
that got us into the Iraq war

00:09:24.296 --> 00:09:25.497
that he claimed to oppose.

00:09:25.497 --> 00:09:27.532
Last week, for example,
the Trump administration

00:09:27.532 --> 00:09:28.867
issued a stunning warning,

00:09:28.867 --> 00:09:30.669
claiming that
"Iran has a robust,

00:09:30.669 --> 00:09:32.738
clandestine
nuclear-weapons program."

00:09:32.738 --> 00:09:34.640
Now the key word there is "has."

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:36.242
The Trump administration
seemed to be saying

00:09:36.242 --> 00:09:38.177
that Iran currently has

00:09:38.177 --> 00:09:40.779
a secret ongoing
nuclear program right now.

00:09:40.779 --> 00:09:43.515
In other words, they're saying
Iran has WMDs.

00:09:43.515 --> 00:09:45.217
If that were true,
it would be massive news.

00:09:45.217 --> 00:09:47.486
But it quickly turned out
it was a mistake.

00:09:47.486 --> 00:09:50.489
-One single word
in a White House statement

00:09:50.489 --> 00:09:53.392
set off
a barrage of alarm and questions

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:55.360
about Iran's nuclear capability.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:59.365
The initial statement
said that Iran "has" --

00:09:59.365 --> 00:10:00.766
present tense --

00:10:00.766 --> 00:10:03.735
a robust, clandestine
nuclear-weapons program.

00:10:03.735 --> 00:10:06.772
An updated statement,
sent a couple of hours later,

00:10:06.772 --> 00:10:10.442
read Iran "had" -- past tense --
such a program.

00:10:10.442 --> 00:10:13.412
The White House claims
that was a "clerical error."

00:10:13.412 --> 00:10:16.148
-Wow, that is a hell of a typo.

00:10:16.148 --> 00:10:18.684
That's like your doctor saying,
"You have 40 days to live.

00:10:18.684 --> 00:10:20.753
Whoops! Sorry --
years, 40 years."

00:10:20.753 --> 00:10:22.121
[ Laughter ]

00:10:22.121 --> 00:10:24.289
So it was a one-letter typo,
which is no small thing.

00:10:24.289 --> 00:10:25.491
If we're not careful,

00:10:25.491 --> 00:10:27.726
we could end up invading
Iraq again by accident.

00:10:27.726 --> 00:10:29.195
[ Laughter ]

00:10:29.195 --> 00:10:31.296
And something tells me
the Trump tweet about that

00:10:31.296 --> 00:10:32.565
will be short.

00:10:32.565 --> 00:10:34.600
[ Laughter ]

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.568
Trump is repeating
the same mistakes that got us

00:10:36.568 --> 00:10:38.870
into the Iraq war,
and he's being cheered on

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:41.340
by many of the same people
who orchestrated that war.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:44.042
In fact, the only lesson Trump
seems to have learned is...

00:10:44.042 --> 00:10:45.744
-You never
go into a bicycle race.

00:10:45.744 --> 00:10:47.479
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:47.479 --> 00:10:51.117
[ Cheers and applause ]

